<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec construction orders down 25.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec construction orders down 25.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's construction orders fell 25.4 percent in December from a year earlier to 1.37 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Construction orders increased 4.8 percent to 20.38 trillion yen in 1996 from a year earlier, it said.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in billions of yen unless specified, with year-on-year changes) of the December construction orders:</p>
<p> Domestic private-sector orders		  754.08  -19.6</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders		   498.98  -35.7</p>
<p> Foreign government facilities in Japan and</p>
<p> orders of less than 10 million yen	     46.13   -1.8</p>
<p> Orders received abroad			     68.13   -5.4</p>
<p> Total						 1.37 trln -25.4</p>
</text>
